{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\n`rebar fsck` reports 8 stray top-level directories in the tickets tracker\n(`/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker`), each flagged twice — once as\n`MISSING_CREATE` (no CREATE event found) and once inside the single\n`FOREIGN_STORE_PATH` finding:\n\n    0efe-9207-2706-43a3  2021-2ef0-e36f-44fc  6f8a-45e5-d9ec-402c  a109-e758-71bb-4371\n    afe5-db0b-e9c5-45d8  c827-81ee-a592-4d27  d052-ad3f-23c1-4511  fa38-670c-d8fc-4c22\n\nBaseline: `fsck complete: 16 issues found` = 8 MISSING_CREATE + 6 STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED\n+ 1 FOREIGN_STORE_PATH + 1 ENV_ID_MISMATCH.\n\n## Evidence (pre-removal triage)\n\nAll 8 are empty directories (`ls -A` returns nothing), none is committed\n(`git ls-tree HEAD <dir>` empty for all 8), `git status --porcelain` in the tracker is\nclean because git cannot track empty directories, and `rebar exists <id>` returns exit 1\nfor all 8. `lsof +D` on the tracker shows no process holding a file under any of the 8.\nDirectory mtimes span 2026-08-10 11:05 to 2026-08-12 12:52 — all far outside the\n~30-minute live-writer window (triage run 2026-08-12 17:59 PDT).\n`rebar tracker-maintenance --status` independently reports `unpushed ticket commits: 0`\nand exactly these 8 as `foreign top-level paths`, so `--clean` will not refuse and the\nbreak-glass `--force` is NOT needed. `rebar review-plan` itself logs each one as\n\"debris of an interrupted write; safe to delete\".\n\n## Likely cause\n\n`os.makedirs(ticket_dir)` succeeded and the process died before the first event was\natomically renamed in — agents interrupted mid-write by host sleeps, session-limit kills,\nand shell-cap timeouts across the active fleet.\n\n## How `--clean` actually behaves (correcting an earlier draft of this plan)\n\n`rebar tracker-maintenance --clean` is ALL-OR-NOTHING over the foreign set:\n`src/rebar/_commands/tracker_maintenance.py` iterates `for name in foreign:` and calls\n`shutil.rmtree(full)` on every entry that `fsck.foreign_store_path_list` returned, with no\nper-directory filter and no CLI surface for passing a subset. The guards below therefore\ndo NOT select what the tool deletes — they are a precondition on running it at all.\nConsequently the guard set is applied as an equality check: immediately before the write,\n`--status`'s foreign list must be exactly the 8 triaged ids. If it lists any 9th path, or\nany triaged directory has become non-empty, the run is ABORTED and reported rather than\nnarrowed — because there is no way to narrow it. This also bounds the check-then-act\n(TOCTOU) window to the gap between that `--status` and the `--clean`, seconds apart.\n\n## Relationship to 043f-3336-d5de-45be (closed)\n\nThat bug made the plan-relation reducer TOLERATE event-less directories and explicitly\nrejected writer-side cleanup, because an automatic rmdir races a concurrent session's\nin-flight write (\"tolerate, never tidy\"). This ticket does not reintroduce automatic\ncleanup: it is a one-off operator-initiated sweep whose guards are precisely the evidence\nan automatic writer-side rmdir could never establish.\n\n## Plan (minimal, deterministic — five guards, all-or-nothing)\n\nPer directory: (1) empty; (2) uncommitted; (3) `rebar exists <id>` exits 1; (4) no open\nfile handle under it; (5) mtime older than 30 minutes. Then the run-level gate: `--status`\nforeign list equals the 8 triaged ids exactly. All six conditions hold -> run\n`rebar tracker-maintenance --clean` (backup ref before first write, refusal on unpushed\nticket commits, durable audit). Any condition fails -> make NO writes and report back.\nNo raw git in the tracker, no stash. `STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED` (benign, auto-resolved) and\n`ENV_ID_MISMATCH` (known by-design flag from change 1638) are out of scope and must not\nbe touched.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: A per-directory triage verdict for all 8 directories is recorded as a comment on\n      this ticket, each citing the five guards. Verified by `rebar show 7c6e-4b8a-59c5-46db`\n      showing a comment naming all 8 ids with a verdict each.\n- [ ] AC2: Immediately before any write, `rebar tracker-maintenance --status` is re-run and\n      its `foreign top-level paths` list is asserted byte-equal to the 8 triaged ids;\n      on any mismatch the sweep is aborted with no writes and the mismatch recorded.\n      Verified by the recorded `--status` output in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] AC3: Given AC2's equality assertion held, `rebar tracker-maintenance --clean` is run\n      and exits 0 having printed a backup ref, and afterwards\n      `rebar fsck 2>&1 | grep -c -E 'MISSING_CREATE|FOREIGN_STORE_PATH'` prints 0.\n      If AC2's assertion failed instead, this criterion is satisfied by recording the abort\n      and making no writes.\n- [ ] AC4: No committed ticket data is modified. Verified by capturing\n      `git -C .tickets-tracker rev-parse HEAD` before and after and asserting the two are\n      byte-identical, and by `git -C .tickets-tracker status --porcelain` staying empty.\n\n## Testing\n\nA store data operation, so verification is by command exit code and before/after diff\nrather than by unit test:\n\n1. Before: `rebar fsck 2>&1 | tail -1` (record issue count);\n   `git -C /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker rev-parse HEAD` (record sha).\n2. Per-directory guards: `ls -A <dir>` empty; `git ls-tree HEAD <dir>` empty;\n   `rebar exists <id>` exit 1; `lsof +D` naming no file under it; mtime > 30 min old.\n3. Run-level gate: `rebar tracker-maintenance --status` foreign list == the 8 ids exactly.\n4. Act: `rebar tracker-maintenance --clean` — must exit 0 and print a backup ref.\n5. After: `rebar fsck 2>&1 | grep -c -E 'MISSING_CREATE|FOREIGN_STORE_PATH'` must print 0;\n   `git -C .tickets-tracker rev-parse HEAD` must equal the step-1 sha;\n   `git -C .tickets-tracker status --porcelain` must be empty."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786583402932505001,"uuid":"e9331840-8adf-40b4-86d8-5d87b12657ed"}